# Migration SQL is checksum-pinned, so its bytes must be identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks the files out as CRLF while git stores LF, and
# a checksum computed from the working tree differs from one computed on a Linux CI runner. That is
# exactly how the immutability gate came to fail in CI while passing locally: nine baseline hashes
# had been recorded from a CRLF working tree.
prisma/migrations/**/migration.sql text eol=lf
